    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0154" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v19/pg122"/>

                <head>70. Memorandum From the President’s Special Assistant (Rostow) to President
                        Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d70-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1967-05-26T11:10:00-04:00">May 26, 1967, 11:10 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. President:</p>
                <p>Herewith our Military Attachés in Tel Aviv state their belief that “Israel is
                    approaching a decision in favor of a preemptive attack”; and they explain
                        why.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d70-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">2½ lines of source text not declassified</hi>]<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d70-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>One underlying problem is, of course, that the Israelis feel that the longer a
                    confrontation over Aqaba is avoided—and the issue is kicked around in the UN—the
                    more their rights in the Straits will become eroded.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Walt </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d70-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d70-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Country File, Middle East
                    Crisis, Vol. II. Top Secret; [<hi rendition="#italic">codeword not
                        declassified</hi>].</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d70-f2" n="2" xml:id="d70-f2-content">
                <p>The attachment conveying this assessment was telegram STRIKE 4553 from
                    CINCSTRIKE, May 26, 0801Z.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d70-f3" n="3" xml:id="d70-f3-content">
